          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: An air traffic controller reports an observation made by a commercial airline pilot en route from Rome to Casablanca. On August 16 at 20:37 UTC, the pilot, overflying Sardinia, observed a yellow glow with debris passing through the atmosphere. At the same time, the air traffic controller at Bastia Tower observed a bright white light. This was a meteor seen by numerous witnesses (104) and cataloged by the International Meteor Organization (IMO). The GEIPAN classifies this case as A: observation of a meteor.",
